# Case of the Shattered Pact {2}. Enters: "search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle" - Bot1 finds
# the Forest (not the Ornithopter) and it is revealed. "To solve - There are five colors among permanents you control": Q, Your Illustrious
# Host ({W}{U}{B}{R}{G}) is all five colors; the Case is colorless. On turn 1 only Q is out, no Case, nothing to solve. On turn 3 the Case enters, and
# at the end step Q makes five colors: the Case becomes solved (CR 719.3a) with Bot2's Ornithopter beside it counting for nothing. Solved: "At the
# beginning of combat on your turn, target creature you control gains flying, double strike, and vigilance until end of turn": on turn 4 (Bot2's
# combat) nothing happens; on turn 5 the trigger targets Q alone (Bot2's Ornithopter is no legal target, so none is asked) and Q has the three keywords at combat and none once the turn is over.

